{"body":"Resolved on main via Path A (per-(rid, release, cid) tag key).\n\nImplemented in:\n- `7750b40` fix(seeder): key seeded tags by release — extends the binary tag key from `(rid, cid)` to `(rid, release, cid)` (`seeded_tag`, `seeded_release_prefix`, `parse_seeded_tag`).\n- `9a5c9f1` refactor: fold seed flag and release into one option — adds the `release` field to the `Command::Unseed { rid, release, cid }` wire message, so the CLI scope reaches the node instead of always sending `Unseed { rid, cid }`.\n\nEnd to end on main: the CLI threads the scope through (`release: release_filter.map(|r| r.oid())`), and the node branches on it — `Some(release) => untag_seeded(...)` deletes just that release tag, `None => untag_all(...)` sweeps every release. So `unseed --release X` now leaves release Y's tag and bytes intact.\n\nFollow-up hardening on the same path (not part of the core fix): `c7d139f` removes a single-release unseed TOCTOU, `93a45e4` bounds `untag_all` to a snapshot of releases so a concurrent seed survives, and the scope-prompt commit makes the unseed-all blast radius explicit.\n\nClosing as resolved.","replyTo":"2d7bca6ae5af90ff71eefcf8b17dc32dd0eb1ece","type":"comment"}